\label{sec:c0}

We define the multi-candidate rate $C_0$ as the fraction of questions for which the $K$ sampled traces produce more than one distinct answer:
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:c0}
C_0 = \frac{|\{q \in \mathcal{Q} : |\mathcal{A}(q)| > 1\}|}{|\mathcal{Q}|}.
\end{equation}

